  "term": "diazepam-binding inhibitor",
  "definition": "Diazepam-binding inhibitor is a small protein present in both the central nervous system and the rest of the body that can displace diazepam from a recognition site on GABA receptors. It also carries certain fatty acid–related molecules and helps regulate lipid metabolism.",
